"""Copy for the device picker, and for a config that carries no obfuscation.

Kept in its own catalogue and merged late in ``i18n`` so these keys win.

The reason this screen exists is worth writing down. An AmneziaWG file is
rejected outright by the official WireGuard app on iOS, so the same button that
worked on Android produced "nothing happens" on an iPhone. The bot cannot see
what phone somebody holds, and guessing it from the language or the operator is
how you ship a file that cannot load. So it asks. One tap, before anything is
built.

``wg.sent_clean`` is the delivery message for a platform that gets standard
WireGuard. It deliberately does not print a junk train, because that file has
none, and it says out loud that obfuscation is off: an iPhone user whose tunnel
dies under DPI deserves to know why and what to install instead.
"""

